-- title:
--   All-layer smooth-point stalks from base-layer stalks (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a place $P$ (a valuation subring of a field, proper, containing the image of the base field and a principal ideal ring) $P.\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of its associated adic valuation.
--
--   **Ambient data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 2$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field of $A$, whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. the rational places $w$ satisfying the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`; the inclusion `hle` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside Laurent series) into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$, that is, a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with its residue field, together with a degree-preserving map on places and the usual scaling and divisor-transport clauses; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a distinguished element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   **Small-constant field.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that the pullback $A \cap k_0 = A.\mathrm{comap}$ along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is henselian local (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`, asserting that every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and elements.** A prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layers.** A type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite-dimensional over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n \subseteq K_n$ with $A_n = A \cap K_n$ (`hAn`); a base layer $K_b$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b \subseteq K_b$ with $A_b = A \cap K_b$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained from $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that
--
--   - (generation) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and
--
--   - (linear disjointness) for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with all $a_i$ in $k_0(\text{image of }K') \sqcup F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$,
--
--   and for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring of integers pulling back to $A$, with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue field of $A$, and satisfying the scaling clause) with $R.\mathrm{integers} \cap F_0 = W_0$, every finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, every family of subrings $S_b(Q) \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, every family of ring homomorphisms $\varphi_b(Q) : A_b[X] \to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q) : S_b(Q) \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and every family of sets $D_b(Q)$ of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$: if
--
--   1. $\#N = q+1$;
--
--   2. for every place $Q \notin N$, the following twelve clauses hold: the image of $A_b$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C a)$ has that image as its value for each $a \in A_b$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C a))$ is the residue in $A$ of that element; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X)) = 0$; $S_b(Q)$ is local with $\ker \chi_b(Q)$ its maximal ideal; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in $k_0(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ and every element $f$ of that field satisfies $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_b(Q)$ with $h \neq 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_b(Q) \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, and an element of $S_b(Q)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ precisely when it is divisible by $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$; for each $f \in S_b(Q)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$ under $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of those places $P$ which are rational, have every $f \in S_b(Q)$ in their valuation subring with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and satisfy $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ less than $1$ if and only if $\chi_b(Q)(f) = 0$;
--
--   3. the discs are pairwise disjoint: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_b(Q)$ and $D_b(Q')$, then $Q = Q'$;
--
--   4. for $Q \notin N$ every $P \in D_b(Q)$ satisfies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, via `hle`, of the base-changed $q$-expansion `coeffEmb _ jq` of $j$;
--
--   5. for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, with $\zeta$ in $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every witness that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$: the translate of $Q$ under the induced residue automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and for $Q \notin N$ one has $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_b(Q)) = D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q)$;
--
--   then there exist families $S_n(Q, n)$ of subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q,n) : A_n[X] \to S_n(Q,n)$ and $\chi_n(Q,n) : S_n(Q,n) \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and sets $D_n(Q,n)$ of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, such that:
--
--   (A) $\#N = q+1$;
--
--   (B) for every $Q \notin N$ and every layer $n$: the map $A_n \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ sending $a$ to the residue of its image in $A$ is surjective; the image of $A_n$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C a)$ equals the image of $a$ for each $a \in A_n$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A_n$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ vanishes there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ fixing the coefficients ($\chi(\varphi_n(C a)) = a$), reducing to $\chi_n(Q,n)$, and sending $\varphi_n(X)$ to $c$; every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and its residue there is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_n(Q,n)$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ with every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ in the valuation subring of $P$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and with $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ less than $1$ if and only if $\chi_n(Q,n)(f) = 0$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) \neq \varphi_n(Q,n)(C c)$ for all $c \in A_n$; $S_n(Q,n)$ is local with maximal ideal the vanishing locus of $\chi_n(Q,n)$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_n(Q,n)$ is contained in $k_0(\text{image of }K_n) \sqcup F_0$ and every element of that field has the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_n(Q,n)$, $h \neq 0$; the linear disjointness clause holds for $K_n$ (for $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K_n$ and $a_i$ in $k_0(\text{image of }K_n) \sqcup F_0$, $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$); every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ fixing the coefficients and reducing to $\chi_n(Q,n)$ has kernel the principal ideal generated by $\varphi_n(X) - \varphi_n(C(\chi(\varphi_n(X))))$; there is a nonzero $\varpi \in A_n$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_n(Q,n)$, such that an element $f$ of $k_0(\text{image of }K_n) \sqcup F_0$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_n(Q,n)$ with $\varphi_n(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_n(Q,n)$ there is a monic $r \in A_n[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ mapped along $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g, h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$. Moreover, for each $Q \notin N$ the layers are compatible: there is a witness that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_n(Q,n) \le S_n(Q,n')$, and then $S_n(Q,n')$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ and the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ coincide for all $n, n'$; and $\chi_n(Q,n')$ restricted along the inclusion $S_n(Q,n) \le S_n(Q,n')$ equals $\chi_n(Q,n)$;
--
--   (C) for $Q, Q' \notin N$, any layer $n$ and any place $P$ lying in both $D_n(Q,n)$ and $D_n(Q',n)$, one has $Q = Q'$;
--
--   (D) for $Q \notin N$, every layer $n$ and every $P \in D_n(Q,n)$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base-changed $q$-expansion of $j$;
--
--   (E) for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every witness that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every place $Q$: the translate of $Q$ under $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and for $Q \notin N$ and every layer $n$, $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_n(Q,n)) = D_n(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q,\,n)$;
--
--   (F) $S_b(Q) \le S_n(Q,n)$ for every $Q \notin N$ and every $n$;
--
--   (G) $D_b(Q) \subseteq D_n(Q,n)$ for every $Q \notin N$ and every $n$.
--
--   This is the layerwise propagation step in the construction of the semistable reduction of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at the prime $q = 2$: étale-local stalk data (coordinate ring, coordinate, residue character and residue disc) given over the base layer $k_0 \cap A$ at each non-end point of the special fibre is extended to every finite layer $K_n$, compatibly along inclusions of layers and containing the base data. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd), where the resulting charts and discs are assembled into the supersingular component picture; the hypotheses involving $\ell_g$, $\ell$, $\zeta_0$ and $\varpi_t$ record the rigid auxiliary level at which the case $q = 2$ is treated.
